think OTHER HAND BEFORE A FILE MOVED. Claude Code is the other hand on the anointed line, most recently the Hush loom lap; this checkout is clean and separate, and every commit in this lap stays path-limited.
think ROTA. N=3821 gives row 1, AIR -- law and boundary through TAME Core, Single-Stranded, and Gauge. The lap presses the boundary between Caravan's living front-door count and the roster that already knows the directory whole.
think REDS FIRST. The cold roster read five reds. Two unchanged guards need ripgrep absent from the pier PATH, so they are a machine limit. Rule twins are custody gate %7. Pond entry is Hush's gated switchover. The stale git nib must travel inside this work commit and may not become a pin-only repair.
think MY FIRST NIB WAS A TREE, NOT A COMMIT. I copied the roster's tree digest into the card and the post-commit nib witness refused it. The empty index and unchanged HEAD permitted the narrow amend. After rebase, upstream's pre-amend sibling was absent from this object store; the same guards refused that floating claim, and the generated-page debt joins its repair in one follow-up commit.
think CLAIM. The five named Caravan optimization-spine moves have landed. The next Caravan crux was its front door: it reported 110 modules and 109 witnesses from 20260824 while the current ladder guard read 114 modules and 114 rows at zero disagreement.
obs THE SEAM IS PROVEN FROM BOTH SIDES. The front door reads 114 modules from the ladder roster and 121 registered witnesses from the choir roster. A pen carrying the same counts passes; changing only the module count refuses, and changing only the witness count refuses.
obs THE MACHINE LIMIT AND TREE DEFECT ARE SEPARATE. The bare pier PATH still lacks rg, and the two affected guards pass unchanged when Nix supplies it. Caravan's stale front-door figures lived in tracked prose and now close on a tracked witness.
obs THE BOUNDARY STAYS SINGLE-STRANDED. The ladder scan owns the module set, the choir scan owns the witness set, and the door guard compares their answers rather than inventing a third census.
